diagnosis_text:
The issue is not a network reachability problem; it is an application/service failure on the Office B server (srv1). From PC1 we can ping srv1 successfully and sustain high throughput (iperf ~83 Mbit/s), proving L2/L3 path, routing, and bandwidth between Office A and B are healthy. However, TCP connection attempts from PC1 to common services on srv1 (22/80/139/445/2049) all fail. The same failures occur from a local Office B client (pc3), ruling out inter-site ACLs and localizing the problem to the server itself.

On srv1, systemd reports key services inactive: apache2 is “Active: inactive (dead)” and sshd is “Active: inactive (dead)”. netstat shows no listeners on 22/80/139/445; only DNS (port 53) is bound on 10.5.0.4
